# Ralph Progress Log — ralph/article-image-blurhash

## Codebase Patterns

- Shared AT Protocol lexicons live under `src/shared/lexicons/`.
  Export literal lexicon objects with `as const satisfies LexiconDoc`, then
  derive record TypeScript types from the lexicon's `record.properties` and
  `record.required` data instead of duplicating field shapes by hand.
- Deterministic AT Protocol subscription rkeys live in
  `src/shared/subscription-rkey.ts`. Canonicalize the feed URL before hashing,
  and keep callers async because the helper uses WebCrypto `crypto.subtle`.
- AT Protocol OAuth scopes live in `AT_PROTOCOL_OAUTH_SCOPE` from
  `src/server/auth/oauth.ts`; use that constant for authorization requests,
  loopback client IDs, and `/oauth/client-metadata.json` so the scope
  surfaces cannot drift.
- OAuth token exchange returns a browser-safe `session` plus server-only
  `credentials`. The callback persists credentials to the user's Durable
  Object through `PUT /internal/oauth/credentials`; the DO stores the record
  under `oauth:credentials` with `ctx.storage.put`.
- Server-side PDS requests should use `src/server/auth/dpop-proof.ts` for
  later DPoP proof JWTs from persisted private JWKs. Pass an already
  base64url-encoded SHA-256 access-token hash as `accessTokenHash`; the
  helper strips query and fragment from `htu` and only exposes public JWK
  members in the JWT header.
- AT Protocol token refresh lives in
  `src/server/auth/token-refresh.ts`. Keep credential persistence injected
  through `persistCredentials` so callers can write through the user's DO;
  the helper returns a typed `reauth_required` result instead of throwing
  token-related auth failures.
- Server-side PDS record writes live in
  `src/server/auth/pds-write-client.ts`. Pass the persisted
  `OAuthCredentialRecord`, inject `persistCredentials`, and let the helper
  sign DPoP proofs, retry one PDS nonce challenge, refresh on auth failure,
  and report sanitized `atproto` errors without token material.
- Adding feed table columns follows the same cross-store pattern as item
  columns: update `TABLES_SQL`, add a guarded RsssUserDO migration and bump
  `USER_DO_MIGRATION_VERSION`, project the column through
  `FEED_SYNC_COLUMNS`, add local OPFS compatibility in
  `ensureFeedTerminalStateColumns`, and persist the field in both
  `pull-sync.ts` and `push-sync.ts` feed upserts. Keep newly projected
  client `Feed` fields optional when existing bootstrap/test payloads may be
  partial.

