## 2026-06-09 13:56 PDT - US-006
Thread: https://ampcode.com/threads/
- What was implemented: Added a DPoP-bound OAuth token refresh helper that
  exchanges the stored refresh token at the authorization server token
  endpoint, retries once when the server returns `use_dpop_nonce` with a
  `DPoP-Nonce` header, persists rotated access/refresh tokens through an
  injected callback, and returns a typed `reauth_required` result for
  unrecoverable auth failures.
- Files changed: src/server/auth/token-refresh.ts,
  test/oauth-token-refresh.ts, test/run-all-tests.mjs, specs/prd.json,
  progress.log
- Verification: `npx esbuild ./test/oauth-token-refresh.ts --bundle
  --platform=node --format=esm
  --external:./src/server/blurhash-runtime.js --external:stripe
  --alias:cloudflare:workers=./test/cloudflare-workers-stub.ts
  --alias:@sentry/cloudflare=./test/sentry-cloudflare-stub.ts |
  node --input-type=module | npx tap-spec`; `npx tsc --noEmit`;
  `npm run lint`
- **Learnings for future iterations:**
  - Token endpoint DPoP proofs do not include `ath`; reserve `ath` for PDS
    requests that send `Authorization: DPoP <access-token>`.
  - The AT Protocol token endpoint reports auth-server nonce challenges as
    JSON `{ error: "use_dpop_nonce" }` plus the `DPoP-Nonce` header; retry
    with that nonce once, then treat continued failure as re-auth required.
  - Injecting `persistCredentials` keeps refresh usable by future PDS-write
    helpers without importing the Worker router or Durable Object stub.
