## 2026-06-09 14:02 PDT - US-007
Thread: https://ampcode.com/threads/
- What was implemented: Added a server-side AT Protocol PDS write client
  with `putRecord`, `createRecord`, and `deleteRecord`. Requests are
  DPoP-bound with the stored private JWK and access-token hash, retry one
  server nonce challenge, refresh expired tokens through the existing
  OAuth refresh helper, replay writes with rotated credentials, and return
  typed `reauth_required` or `pds_write_failed` results. Added focused
  tests for signing, nonce retry, refresh replay, and sanitized error
  reporting, then registered the test in the full harness.
- Files changed: src/server/auth/pds-write-client.ts,
  test/pds-write-client.ts, test/run-all-tests.mjs, specs/prd.json,
  progress.log
- Verification: `npx esbuild ./test/pds-write-client.ts --bundle
  --platform=node --format=esm
  --external:./src/server/blurhash-runtime.js --external:stripe
  --alias:cloudflare:workers=./test/cloudflare-workers-stub.ts
  --alias:@sentry/cloudflare=./test/sentry-cloudflare-stub.ts |
  node --input-type=module | npx tap-spec`; `npm run lint`;
  `npx tsc --noEmit`; `npm test`
- **Learnings for future iterations:**
  - Use `pds-write-client.ts` for all authenticated repo writes instead of
    hand-rolling PDS fetches in feature endpoints.
  - PDS write tests can stay hermetic by injecting `fetch`,
    `persistCredentials`, `now`, and `reportError`.
  - Error reporting context should include operation, collection, status,
    and server error strings, but never OAuth access or refresh tokens.
